00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.150 align:start position:0%
over a dozen former russian mcdonald's  locations reopened this past weekend  with different branding and a new name  bukushnu and tuchka or tasty and that's  it this comes after the american fast  food icon permanently left russia last  month following its invasion of ukraine  mcdonald said last month it would sell  847 russian locations to alexander gavor  who operated 24 franchise locations in  siberia  gavor who built his fortune in russia's  coal and oil sectors would not tell  forbes russia in a recent interview how  much he paid for the restaurants but he  did say he had competition and he hopes  to expand to 1 000 restaurants in the  country within the next few years the  menu in the new stores is largely  similar but they cannot sell branded  items such as big macs or mcflurries due  to trademarks mcdonald's holds  historical significance in russia as it  was one of the first western brands to  open in the former soviet union the  first location opened in 1990 and  moscow's pushkin square shortly after  the fall of the berlin wall that  location and 14 others opened up on june  12th with the new name and branding 50  more debuted on june 13th the new  company told reuters they plan to have  all of the former russian mcdonald's  locations transformed by the end of  summer
 

